  "details": "Cockpit enables users to administer GNU/Linux servers using a web browser. It offers network configuration, log inspection, diagnostic reports, SELinux troubleshooting, interactive command-line sessions, and more.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * cockpit: Cockpit: Local privilege escalation via insecure symlink handling in public key addition helper (CVE-2026-91151)\n  * cockpit: cockpit: Denial of Service via unbounded fragmented WebSocket messages (CVE-2026-91150)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
